CORE gcc-only
main.c
--arch arm64 --unwind 2 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
--
The AArch64 inline assembly in main.c is interpreted exactly: if CBMC
approximated any statement, the assertions, which check values observed with
an emulator, would fail. A store-exclusive may fail spuriously, so the retry
loops of load-exclusive/store-exclusive sequences are bounded; the executions
that retry more often reach the same states.
